From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:40:49 +0300
Subject: nv30: compiled programs in the disk shader cache (NV30_SHADER_CACHE,
 off by default)

Mesa's GL layer caches a program's NIR, so a warm start skips the GLSL compile and link, but nv30
then still ran nir_to_tgsi at every shader creation and the nvfx translation to RSX code at the
first validate of each program (and again for a vertex program whenever the bound fragment
program's texcoord mapping or the enabled clip planes change): what the start-up profiles call
shader.backend, at every start, warm or not. With NV30_SHADER_CACHE=on both results go into the
screen's disk cache, which nouveau_screen.c already creates keyed by the driver binary's build id
and the chipset, so any Mesa rebuild or another GPU misses every entry (MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR,
_DISABLE and _MAX_SIZE apply as to the rest of the cache):

- TGSI (nv30_fp_state_create, nv30_vp_state_create): key the serialized NIR the state tracker
  hands over plus the stage; value the TGSI tokens nir_to_tgsi made of it. A hit frees the NIR
  as nir_to_tgsi would have.
- Fragment programs: key the TGSI tokens, the 3D class and NV40_FP_EXPORT32; value the code as
  translated (the constants are patched in at validate, as before), its constant slots, the
  texcoord mapping and the control words (FP_CONTROL, coord conventions, RT_ENABLE, texcoords,
  vp_or, point sprite control).
- Vertex programs: key the TGSI tokens, the class, the texcoord mapping taken from the fragment
  program and the enabled clip planes; value the code before relocation, the constants and
  immediates, the branch and constant relocations and the input/output masks.

Only a program in its initial state uses the cache (a failed translation leaves a partial one
behind and is translated as before); an entry that doesn't parse is ignored. The words the
translations OR into are stored as a new program's, so a hit gives what a translation gives.
NV30_SHADER_CACHE_STATS=1 prints a "nv30-shcache:" line at context destruction and at exit (process
totals; games often exit without destroying their context): hits, misses and
the ms each took, for TGSI, fragment and vertex programs; counted with the cache off as well,
where every creation is a miss and the miss ms is what the cache could save.

Forwarded: no

